---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Pricing — AI Web" description="AI Web credit-based research pricing is coming soon.">
  <div class="page-shell pricing-page">
    <div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Simple by design</p><h1>Research on your terms.</h1><p>AI Web is designed around prepaid analysis credits. We’re validating launch pricing now so the model is clear, useful and sustainable.</p></div>
    <div class="pricing-grid"><article class="pricing-card pricing-card--featured"><p class="pricing-label">Launch access</p><h2>Credit packs</h2><p class="pricing-copy">Purchase credits when you need them. No subscription decision required.</p><div class="pricing-placeholder"><span>Launch pricing</span><strong>Coming soon</strong></div><a class="button button--primary" href="/auth">Create an account <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><small>Payments are not enabled in this preview.</small></article><article class="pricing-card"><p class="pricing-label">Included today</p><h2>Explore the foundation</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><span>✓</span> Multi-agent research workflow</li><li><span>✓</span> Bull and bear perspectives</li><li><span>✓</span> Account-based saved history</li><li><span>✓</span> Credits shown in your workspace</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div>
    <section class="pricing-note"><p class="eyebrow">A considered start</p><h2>No invented numbers.<br /><span>Just a clear direction.</span></h2><p>Pricing, payments and credit purchases will be introduced after the analysis experience is ready to support them.</p></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
